" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></summary><div><a href="/nyc/brooklyn/">Brooklyn</a><a href="/nyc/manhattan/">Manhattan</a><a href="/nyc/brooklyn/#williamsburg">Williamsburg &amp; DUMBO</a><a href="/nyc/manhattan/#midtown">Midtown &amp; Chelsea</a></div></details><a href="/nyc/projects/">Projects</a><a href="/nyc/about/">About</a><a href="/nyc/resources/">Resources</a></nav><a class="btn primary header-quote" href="/nyc/contact/">Request a quote <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><details class="export-mobile"><summary>Menu</summary><nav><a href="/nyc/">Home</a><a href="/nyc/products/">Products</a><a href="/nyc/interior-signs/">Interior Signs</a><a href="/nyc/exterior-signs/">Exterior Signs</a><a href="/nyc/vehicle-wraps/">Vehicle Wraps</a><a href="/nyc/custom-signs/">Custom Signs</a><a href="/nyc/trade-show-displays/">Trade Show Displays</a><a href="/nyc/retractable-banners/">Retractable Banners</a><a href="/nyc/brooklyn/">Brooklyn</a><a href="/nyc/manhattan/">Manhattan</a><a href="/nyc/projects/">Projects</a><a href="/nyc/gallery/">Gallery</a><a href="/nyc/resources/">Resources</a><a href="/nyc/contact/">Contact</a></nav></details></div></header><div class="product-ribbon"><div class="wrap"><a href="/nyc/interior-signs/">Interior signs</a><a href="/nyc/exterior-signs/">Exterior signs</a><a href="/nyc/vehicle-wraps/">Vehicle wraps</a><a href="/nyc/custom-signs/">Custom signs</a><a href="/nyc/trade-show-displays/">Trade show displays</a><a href="/nyc/retractable-banners/">Retractable banners</a></div></div><main><section class="wrap product-hero"><div><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/nyc/">New York</a> / Decorative window film and privacy graphics</p><p class="eyebrow">VISION GRAPHICS · NEW YORK</p><h1>Decorative window film and privacy graphics</h1><p class="lead">Glass helps an office feel open, but meeting rooms and work areas sometimes need a more deliberate balance of visibility and privacy. Decorative film can add bands, patterns or a frosted appearance that works with the room rather than covering every pane. For New York interiors, Vision Graphics can help develop an approach around where people sit, stand and pass through. Review the glass, lighting and desired effect first, then decide which areas should be screened and which should stay clear.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="#request-quote">Discuss your project <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="#options">Explore options <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></div><figure class="project-image product-photo"><img src="/nyc/assets/mcs-new-corporate-lobby-signs-business-lobby-signage-960.webp" srcset="/nyc/assets/mcs-new-corporate-lobby-signs-business-lobby-signage-480.webp 480w, /nyc/assets/mcs-new-corporate-lobby-signs-business-lobby-signage-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 50vw" alt="Signage example related to Decorative window film and privacy graphics" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Illustrative sign example · Michigan Custom Signs source</figcaption></figure></section><section class="wrap section article-layout"><article><section><h2>Privacy begins with sightlines</h2><p>Photograph the glass from the corridor and from inside the room. A band placed for seated occupants may not address views from a standing position. Use the actual furniture arrangement to judge the proposed pattern, and consider door identification and adjacent panels as one composition.</p></section><section><h2>Separate decorative goals from performance claims</h2><p>Decorative graphics do not automatically establish a thermal, safety or security rating. If those functions are part of the brief, identify them separately and request verified product documentation. Confirm glass compatibility, edge details and cleaning guidance for the specified material before proceeding.</p></section><section><h2>Choose the coverage you actually need</h2><p>Decide whether the goal is privacy at desk height, screening for an entire meeting room or a repeated brand pattern. Compare a continuous frosted band with individual shapes or printed imagery. A larger covered area is not automatically the better solution: preserve useful views and review the effect from both sides of the glass under typical lighting.</p></section><section><h2>What affects the quote and installation scope</h2><p>The number and size of panes, material, pattern complexity and amount of existing film to remove affect the scope. Tall glass, furniture that limits access, door hardware and restricted work hours can add installation work. Confirm who will move furniture, clean or prepare the glass, remove old material and arrange building access. Installation and removal should be stated separately in the quote.</p></section><section><h2>What to send for a window-film quote</h2><p>Send a wide photograph of each glass wall, approximate pane dimensions, a pane count and the project address or ZIP. Add close-ups of existing film, handles and any markings, plus your logo if branding is needed. Explain which views you want to screen, your target date and available installation hours. Final material selection and measurements need review before production.</p></section><section id="options"><p class="eyebrow">MATERIALS &amp; APPROACHES</p><h2>Find the right fit.</h2><div class="options-grid"><div><h3>Frosted appearance bands</h3><p>Screen a chosen sightline across doors and fixed panels. Review the band height from seated and standing positions.</p></div><div><h3>Full-panel decorative film</h3><p>Create a more continuous screened surface where broad coverage suits the room. Confirm the appearance under the actual lighting.</p></div><div><h3>Cut patterns and logos</h3><p>Repeat brand elements or geometric shapes while leaving selected areas transparent. Detailed artwork and alignment affect production planning.</p></div><div><h3>Printed decorative designs</h3><p>Introduce imagery or color across one pane or a series of panels. Plan joins, door gaps and the appearance from the reverse side.</p></div></div></section><section><h2>Where it can work</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Meeting and conference rooms</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Street-level consultation spaces</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Glass office partitions</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Reception and tenant-entry glass</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Office relocations and privacy refreshes</li></ul></section><section class="faqs"><h2>A few useful answers.</h2><details><summary>Does decorative film make a room fully private?<span>+</span></summary><p>The effect depends on the material, pattern, lighting and viewpoint. Review the desired level of screening before selecting it.</p></details><details><summary>Can the same pattern continue across several panes?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes, a measured elevation helps align the pattern while accounting for mullions, gaps, handles and door movement.</p></details><details><summary>Can you replace existing window film?<span>+</span></summary><p>Replacement can be reviewed. Share photographs and, if known, the age and type of existing film. Removal time, adhesive residue, glass condition and access affect the scope; removal is not assumed to be included.</p></details><details><summary>Does privacy film also reduce heat or provide security?<span>+</span></summary><p>Decorative privacy and other performance needs are separate specifications. Explain any heat, glare, safety or security goal so the proposed product documentation can be reviewed. Do not infer those properties from a frosted appearance.</p></details></section></article><aside class="product-aside"><p class="eyebrow">LET’S START WITH THE DETAILS</p><h3>Have a space in mind?</h3><p>A photo, a few measurements and your project ZIP help us ask the right questions.</p><a href="/nyc/contact/?photo=1" class="btn dark"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-camera" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.997 4a2 2 0 0 1 1.76 1.05l.486.9A2 2 0 0 0 18.003 7H20a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V9a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h1.997a2 2 0 0 0 1.759-1.048l.489-.904A2 2 0 0 1 10.004 4z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3"></circle></svg> Send a project photo</a><hr><h3>Related possibilities</h3><a href="/nyc/window-graphics/">Window graphics<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/office-signs/">Office signs<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/environmental-graphics/">Environmental graphics<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/lobby-signs/">Lobby signs<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a h